
::Stored procedure Objectives::
To produce a stored procedure, which of the following statement is used?
{
    ~CREATE FUNCTION
    ~PRODUCE FUNCTION
    ~PROVIDE PROCEDURE
    =CREATE PROCEDURE
}

::Stored procedures::
Stored functions are defined to send their output to a ____ and stored procedures are designed to return outputs to ____.
{
    ~ the console, view
    = query, the application
    ~ view, the console
    ~ the application, query
}

::Stored procedures::
Which procedure parameter enables the caller to pass in a value and get back a value?
{
    =INOUT
    ~IN
    ~OUT
    ~OUTIN
}

::Stored procedures::
Which of the following is used to call a stored procedure?
{
    ~ select
    = call
    ~ set
    ~ execute
}
